From 54f2f51f5233026e608f8235f5377b9b473918e3, amended locally
Subject: [PATCH] spa: libcamera: device: 0.8 compatibility (amended)

Carries upstream commit 54f2f51f5233026e608f8235f5377b9b473918e3
("spa: libcamera: device: 0.8 compatibility", Barnabás Pőcze), merged
to pipewire master after the 1.6.11 tag, plus one local amendment:

the version guard relies on LIBCAMERA_VERSION_MAJOR and
LIBCAMERA_VERSION_MINOR, which are defined in libcamera/version.h —
a header that spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp never
included. Without the include, the macros evaluate to 0 in the
preprocessor, the guard selects the #else (pre-0.8) branch, and
compilation against libcamera 0.8 fails with the original enum
errors. The amendment adds the include so the guard can see the
installed libcamera version (MAJOR=0, MINOR=8), while 0.7
compatibility is preserved via the #else branch.
---
 spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp
--- a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp
+++ b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 
 #include <libcamera/camera.h>
 #include <libcamera/property_ids.h>
+#include <libcamera/version.h>
 
 using namespace libcamera;
 
@@ -69,12 +70,21 @@
 {
 	if (auto location = camera.properties().get(properties::Location)) {
 		switch (location.value()) {
+#if LIBCAMERA_VERSION_MAJOR > 0 || (LIBCAMERA_VERSION_MAJOR == 0 && LIBCAMERA_VERSION_MINOR >= 8)
+		case properties::LocationFront:
+			return "front";
+		case properties::LocationBack:
+			return "back";
+		case properties::LocationExternal:
+			return "external";
+#else
 		case properties::CameraLocationFront:
 			return "front";
 		case properties::CameraLocationBack:
 			return "back";
 		case properties::CameraLocationExternal:
 			return "external";
+#endif
 		}
 	}
 
